# Copy to .env (git-ignored) and fill in. Real environment variables win.

# Required: the API refuses to start without it.
OPENAI_API_KEY=

# System instructions for the assistant: orient and limit its behavior.
# Optional; without it, it is a helpful assistant that answers the user's
# requests (DEFAULT_CHAT_INSTRUCTIONS in src/chat/domain/chat-instructions.ts).
# Use double quotes for several lines:
# CHAT_INSTRUCTIONS="You are VAM, a cooking assistant.
# Only answer questions about cooking and recipes; politely decline anything else."

# Models the chat may use, comma separated; the first is the default.
# CHAT_MODELS=gpt-5.4-mini,gpt-5.4-nano,gpt-5.4

# Web app origins allowed to use the session cookie (default: the Next.js
# dev server, http://localhost:3001; nothing when NODE_ENV=production).
# WEB_ORIGINS=http://localhost:3001

# SQLite file (default .db/data.sqlite3).
# DB_STORAGE=.db/data.sqlite3
